    },
    "body": "I like this in general. We should think through the integration story with other specs, particularly performance timing specs.\r\n\r\nCan you tell us more about where you want to use it?\r\n\r\nWe should probably add some note explaining that if the time is exposed to developers, you likely want to use the stuff in High Resolution Time (e.g. relative high resolution time).\r\n\r\nHow does this relate to https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#sec-monotonic-clock , and to monotonic time in general? In particular, can multiple invocations of [=now=] ever end up in a situation where the second one returns a value below the first?\r\n\r\nI guess \"[DOMHighResTimeStamp](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dom-domhighrestimestamp) representing the high resolution time at which the [shared monotonic clock](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-shared-monotonic-clock) is zero\" is supposed to be the Unix epoch?\r\n\r\nAnd I guess \"[unsafe shared current time](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-unsafe-shared-current-time)\" might be [=now=]?",
    "state": "COMMENTED",
